"verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "2nd round trip (rare)", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e835", "type": "text", "x": 120, "y": 16254.0, "width": 984.6, "height": 63.8, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#495057", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 1217374575, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 574808104, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "Fast path: (1) and (2) never touch Redis. Only a node that has run out of local permits pays a round trip - and then for a whole\nbatch.\nDenials are served from the negative cache until retryAfter, so an abused key stops generating Redis load at all.", "fontSize": 17, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "Fast path: (1) and (2) never touch Redis. Only a node that has run out of local permits pays a round trip - and then for a whole\nbatch.\nDenials are served from the negative cache until retryAfter, so an abused key stops generating Redis load at all.", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e836", "type": "rectangle", "x": 60, "y": 16724.0, "width": 2280, "height": 71.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#f59e0b", "backgroundColor": "#fff3bf", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g156"], "frameId": null, "roundness": {"type": 3}, "seed": 800949213, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 545582188, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false}, {"id": "e837", "type": "text", "x": 74, "y": 16738.0, "width": 391.1, "height": 17.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#b45309", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g156"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 1584987739, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 559065266, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "THE TRADE-OFF - BOUNDED BY BATCH X NODECOUNT", "fontSize": 14, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "THE TRADE-OFF - BOUNDED BY BATCH X NODECOUNT", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e838", "type": "text", "x": 74, "y": 16761.5, "width": 2002.1, "height": 20.0, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g156"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 427757468, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 943599519, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "A node can hold unspent borrowed permits when traffic shifts, so the effective global rate is slightly under the limit, and a crashing node strands its borrowed permits until the bucket refills. Both are bounded by batch * nodeCount. Size the batch so that bound is acceptable.", "fontSize": 16, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "A node can hold unspent borrowed permits when traffic shifts, so the effective global rate is slightly under the limit, and a crashing node strands its borrowed permits until the bucket refills. Both are bounded by batch * nodeCount. Size the batch so that bound is acceptable.", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e839", "type": "rectangle", "x": 60, "y": 16835.5, "width": 1120, "height": 1121.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#313244", "backgroundColor": "#1e1e2e", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g157"], "frameId": null, "roundness": {"type": 3}, "seed": 531350006, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 398865925, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false}, {"id": "e840", "type": "text", "x": 74, "y": 16849.5, "width": 231.4, "height": 20.0, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#7fd1c4", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g157"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 526864279, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 505741023, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "tiered.js   -   L1 local - L2 Redis", "fontSize": 16, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "tiered.js   -   L1 local - L2 Redis", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e841", "type": "text", "x": 74, "y": 16875.5, "width": 699.2, "height": 1067.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#cdd6f4", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g157"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 329256913, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 604203320, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "/**\n * DECORATOR over any strategy. Two ideas:\n *  1. Negative cache - if Redis said \"blocked until T\", stop asking until T.\n *  2. Batched borrow  - claim `batch` permits in one call, spend them locally.\n *\n * Trade: a node can hold unspent borrowed permits when traffic shifts, so the\n * effective global rate is slightly under the limit, and a crashing node\n * strands its borrowed permits until the bucket refills. Both are bounded by\n * `batch * nodeCount`. Size the batch so that bound is acceptable.\n */\nclass TieredLimiter extends RateLimitStrategy {\n  constructor({ inner, clock = SystemClock, batch = 10, maxKeys = 100_000 }) {\n    super();\n    this.inner  = inner;\n    this.clock  = clock;\n    this.batch  = batch;\n    this.local  = new LruMap(maxKeys);   // key -> { permits, blockedUntil, limit }\n  }\n\n  async consume(key, rule, cost = 1) {\n    const now   = this.clock.now();\n    const entry = this.local.get(key) ?? { permits: 0, blockedUntil: 0 };\n\n    // (1) negative cache: the cheapest possible denial\n    if (entry.blockedUntil > now) {\n      return Decision.deny({\n        ruleId: rule.id, limit: rule.limit, remaining: 0,\n        resetMs: entry.blockedUntil - now, retryAfterMs: entry.blockedUntil - now,\n      });\n    }\n\n    // (2) spend a locally-held permit - zero network\n    if (entry.permits >= cost) {\n      entry.permits -= cost;\n      this.local.set(key, entry);\n      return Decision.allow({ ruleId: rule.id, limit: rule.limit,\n                              remaining: entry.permits, resetMs: rule.windowMs });\n    }\n\n    // (3) refill from L2: borrow a batch in one round trip\n    const want = Math.max(cost, this.batch);\n    const d    = await this.inner.consume(key, rule, want);\n\n    if (d.allowed) {\n      entry.permits      = want - cost;\n      entry.blockedUntil = 0;\n      this.local.set(key, entry);\n      return Decision.allow({ ...d, remaining: entry.permits });\n    }\n\n    // Borrowing the whole batch failed - fall back to asking for just this one\n    // request, so a large batch never causes a false denial.\n    const single = await this.inner.consume(key, rule, cost);\n    if (!single.allowed) {\n      entry.permits      = 0;\n      entry.blockedUntil = now + Math.max(single.retryAfterMs, 50);\n      this.local.set(key, entry);\n    }\n    return single;\n  }\n}", "fontSize": 14, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "/**\n * DECORATOR over any strategy. Two ideas:\n *  1. Negative cache - if Redis said \"blocked until T\", stop asking until T.\n *  2. Batched borrow  - claim `batch` permits in one call, spend them locally.\n *\n * Trade: a node can hold unspent borrowed permits when traffic shifts, so the\n * effective global rate is slightly under the limit, and a crashing node\n * strands its borrowed permits until the bucket refills. Both are bounded by\n * `batch * nodeCount`. Size the batch so that bound is acceptable.\n */\nclass TieredLimiter extends RateLimitStrategy {\n  constructor({ inner, clock = SystemClock, batch = 10, maxKeys = 100_000 }) {\n    super();\n    this.inner  = inner;\n    this.clock  = clock;\n    this.batch  = batch;\n    this.local  = new LruMap(maxKeys);   // key -> { permits, blockedUntil, limit }\n  }\n\n  async consume(key, rule, cost = 1) {\n    const now   = this.clock.now();\n    const entry = this.local.get(key) ?? { permits: 0, blockedUntil: 0 };\n\n    // (1) negative cache: the cheapest possible denial\n    if (entry.blockedUntil > now) {\n      return Decision.deny({\n        ruleId: rule.id, limit: rule.limit, remaining: 0,\n        resetMs: entry.blockedUntil - now, retryAfterMs: entry.blockedUntil - now,\n      });\n    }\n\n    // (2) spend a locally-held permit - zero network\n    if (entry.permits >= cost) {\n      entry.permits -= cost;\n      this.local.set(key, entry);\n      return Decision.allow({ ruleId: rule.id, limit: rule.limit,\n                              remaining: entry.permits, resetMs: rule.windowMs });\n    }\n\n    // (3) refill from L2: borrow a batch in one round trip\n    const want = Math.max(cost, this.batch);\n    const d    = await this.inner.consume(key, rule, want);\n\n    if (d.allowed) {\n      entry.permits      = want - cost;\n      entry.blockedUntil = 0;\n      this.local.set(key, entry);\n      return Decision.allow({ ...d, remaining: entry.permits });\n    }\n\n    // Borrowing the whole batch failed - fall back to asking for just this one\n    // request, so a large batch never causes a false denial.\n    const single = await this.inner.consume(key, rule, cost);\n    if (!single.allowed) {\n      entry.permits      = 0;\n      entry.blockedUntil = now + Math.max(single.retryAfterMs, 50);\n      this.local.set(key, entry);\n    }\n    return single;\n  }\n}", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e842", "type": "text", "x": 1220, "y": 16831.5, "width": 342.9, "height": 27.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#6741d9", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 1898735925, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 1948987929, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "Sharded counters for a whale key", "fontSize": 22, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "Sharded counters for a whale key", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e843", "type": "rectangle", "x": 1220, "y": 16875.5, "width": 1120, "height": 561.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#313244", "backgroundColor": "#1e1e2e", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g158"], "frameId": null, "roundness": {"type": 3}, "seed": 1241848476, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 404264090, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false}, {"id": "e844", "type": "text", "x": 1234, "y": 16889.5, "width": 109.0, "height": 20.0, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#7fd1c4", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g158"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 700805345, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 139165732, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "sharded-key.js", "fontSize": 16, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "sharded-key.js", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e845", "type": "text", "x": 1234, "y": 16915.5, "width": 724.4, "height": 507.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#cdd6f4", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g158"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 850552987, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 540422298, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "/**\n * Split one very hot key across N Redis slots. Each shard enforces limit/N.\n * Accuracy cost: a client whose requests hash unevenly can be denied while the\n * global count is under limit. Mitigate by picking the shard at random rather\n * than by request hash, so the distribution self-balances.\n */\nclass ShardedKeyStrategy extends RateLimitStrategy {\n  constructor({ inner, shards = 8, hotKeys }) {\n    super();\n    this.inner   = inner;\n    this.shards  = shards;\n    this.hotKeys = hotKeys;      // Set, maintained by a heavy-hitter detector\n  }\n\n  async consume(key, rule, cost = 1) {\n    if (!this.hotKeys.has(key)) return this.inner.consume(key, rule, cost);\n\n    const i       = Math.floor(Math.random() * this.shards);\n    const subRule = new Rule({ ...rule, limit: Math.ceil(rule.limit / this.shards),\n                                        burst: Math.ceil(rule.burst / this.shards) });\n    return this.inner.consume(`${key}#${i}`, subRule, cost);\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Heavy-hitter detection off the hot path: sample decisions into a\n * count-min sketch, promote anything above a threshold, decay every minute.\n * Never scan Redis for hot keys - use the traffic you already see.\n */", "fontSize": 14, "fontFamily": 3, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "/**\n * Split one very hot key across N Redis slots. Each shard enforces limit/N.\n * Accuracy cost: a client whose requests hash unevenly can be denied while the\n * global count is under limit. Mitigate by picking the shard at random rather\n * than by request hash, so the distribution self-balances.\n */\nclass ShardedKeyStrategy extends RateLimitStrategy {\n  constructor({ inner, shards = 8, hotKeys }) {\n    super();\n    this.inner   = inner;\n    this.shards  = shards;\n    this.hotKeys = hotKeys;      // Set, maintained by a heavy-hitter detector\n  }\n\n  async consume(key, rule, cost = 1) {\n    if (!this.hotKeys.has(key)) return this.inner.consume(key, rule, cost);\n\n    const i       = Math.floor(Math.random() * this.shards);\n    const subRule = new Rule({ ...rule, limit: Math.ceil(rule.limit / this.shards),\n                                        burst: Math.ceil(rule.burst / this.shards) });\n    return this.inner.consume(`${key}#${i}`, subRule, cost);\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Heavy-hitter detection off the hot path: sample decisions into a\n * count-min sketch, promote anything above a threshold, decay every minute.\n * Never scan Redis for hot keys - use the traffic you already see.\n */", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e846", "type": "rectangle", "x": 1220, "y": 17461.0, "width": 1120, "height": 111.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#22c55e", "backgroundColor": "#d3f9d8", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g159"], "frameId": null, "roundness": {"type": 3}, "seed": 2131267423, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 528171948, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false}, {"id": "e847", "type": "text", "x": 1234, "y": 17475.0, "width": 160.6, "height": 17.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#15803d", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g159"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 1089471102, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 1130239437, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "THE LINE THAT LANDS", "fontSize": 14, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "THE LINE THAT LANDS", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e848", "type": "text", "x": 1234, "y": 17498.5, "width": 1090.6, "height": 60.0, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g159"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 496886794, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 1395092684, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "\"Rate limiting is one of the few places where you can trade accuracy for latency on purpose, because the requirement is already an approximation.\nNobody's SLA says exactly 1000 requests - it says roughly 1000. So I'd size the local batch by how much overshoot the product tolerates, and make\nthat number a config, not a constant.\"", "fontSize": 16, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "\"Rate limiting is one of the few places where you can trade accuracy for latency on purpose, because the requirement is already an approximation.\nNobody's SLA says exactly 1000 requests - it says roughly 1000. So I'd size the local batch by how much overshoot the product tolerates, and make\nthat number a config, not a constant.\"", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e975", "type": "rectangle", "x": 0, "y": 18117.0, "width": 2400, "height": 2546.2, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "transparent", "backgroundColor": "#d3f9d8", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 32, "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "roundness": {"type": 3}, "seed": 959472916, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 1081426380, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false}, {"id": "e850", "type": "rectangle", "x": 60, "y": 18157.0, "width": 64, "height": 40, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#0b7285", "backgroundColor": "#ffffff", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 2, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g160"], "frameId": null, "roundness": {"type": 3}, "seed": 1403008090, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 996251367, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false}, {"id": "e851", "type": "text", "x": 74, "y": 18164.0, "width": 29.8, "height": 30.0, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#0b7285", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g160"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 2128061066, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 79506594, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "08", "fontSize": 24, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "08", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e852", "type": "text", "x": 144, "y": 18159.0, "width": 226.1, "height": 42.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g160"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 219757212, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 9646716, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "Failure modes", "fontSize": 34, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "Failure modes", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e853", "type": "text", "x": 60, "y": 18219.0, "width": 982.2, "height": 22.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#495057", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": [], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 1019545261, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 1895852301, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "The most common way a rate limiter causes an outage is by being the thing that breaks. Design for its own failure first.", "fontSize": 18, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "The most common way a rate limiter causes an outage is by being the thing that breaks. Design for its own failure first.", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e854", "type": "rectangle", "x": 60, "y": 18269.5, "width": 2280, "height": 33.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#adb5bd", "backgroundColor": "#e9ecef", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 0, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g161"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 1759009670, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 496312590, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false}, {"id": "e855", "type": "text", "x": 69, "y": 18277.5, "width": 46.5, "height": 17.5, "angle": 0, "strokeColor": "#495057", "backgroundColor": "transparent", "fillStyle": "solid", "strokeWidth": 1, "strokeStyle": "solid", "roughness": 1, "opacity": 100, "groupIds": ["g161"], "frameId": null, "roundness": null, "seed": 1805081041, "version": 1, "versionNonce": 962710805, "isDeleted": false, "boundElements": null, "updated": 1792011375077, "link": null, "locked": false, "text": "Failure", "fontSize": 14, "fontFamily": 2, "textAlign": "left", "verticalAlign": "top", "containerId": null, "originalText": "Failure", "autoResize": true, "lineHeight": 1.25}, {"id": "e856", "type":